---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { distances } from "../content";
---
<Layout
  title="Location"
  description="Where Palm Central sits on Palm Jebel Ali's master plan, and real drive times to Dubai Marina, Downtown, and both airports."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Location</p>
    <h1>The Spine, between Fronds M and N</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Palm Jebel Ali's master plan splits into five zones — Trunk, Spine,
      Fronds, Crown, and the Crescents — and Palm Central sits on the
      Spine, the section built for community and retail rather than the
      private villa plots on the fronds either side of it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Why the Spine specifically</h2>
    <p>
      The Fronds on Palm Jebel Ali are villa land — large private plots,
      not apartment buildings. The Spine is the through-road connecting the
      whole island back to the mainland, and it's where Nakheel has put
      the community-scale buildings: retail, schools, and — with Palm
      Central — the island's first apartment product. That's a structural
      fact about the master plan, not a marketing choice: if you want an
      apartment on Palm Jebel Ali rather than a villa, the Spine is
      currently the only place that exists.
    </p>
    <p>
      At full build-out, Palm Jebel Ali will be roughly twice the size of
      Palm Jumeirah, with seven islands, sixteen fronds, and over 90km of
      beachfront — a scale that puts Palm Central's current three buildings
      as an early, relatively small piece of a much larger island. Worth
      knowing before assuming the neighbourhood you see today is close to
      finished.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Drive times from Palm Central</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>To</th><th>Drive time</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {distances.map((d) => (
            <tr><td>{d.to}</td><td>{d.time}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What that actually means day to day</h2>
    <p>
      Palm Jebel Ali is closer to Jebel Ali Port, Al Maktoum International
      Airport, and the Expo City side of Dubai than it is to Downtown or
      DIFC. If your work or school routine runs through the older, more
      central part of the city, the 20–25 minute drive to Downtown is the
      number that matters more than the shorter trip to the airport. If
      your life already leans toward the Marina, JBR, or the newer
      Jebel Ali / Expo corridor, the location reads differently — closer
      to the centre of gravity than the "new island, far from everything"
      framing some listings default to.
    </p>
    <p>
      There's no confirmed public transit link to the island yet; a car
      (yours or a taxi) is the realistic way in and out for the foreseeable
      future, same as most new Dubai coastal developments at this stage of
      build-out.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container cta">
    <h2>Want the price list next?</h2>
    <p>
      See <a href="/prices/" title="Palm Central price list, both phases">current pricing</a> for
      the phase that's actually for sale, or <a href="/#interest" title="Register interest in Palm Central">register your interest</a> directly.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .cta { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
</style>
